WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
One governed supply-chain workflow now runs through three conversational host models.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.900
Gemini Enterprise renders native A2UI delivered over A2A.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.400
ChatGPT and Claude render the same Oracle-backed results as an MCP App.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.900
The video is silent and fully captioned.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.400
The host adapter changes, but the governed core does not.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.900
Gemini Enterprise calls an A2A agent carrying declarative A2UI.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.400
ChatGPT and Claude call a Streamable HTTP MCP server carrying a sandboxed HTML resource.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.900
Every path reaches the same Java service, Toolkit, and Oracle AI Database.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.900
The Java service launches a pinned Oracle Database MCP Java Toolkit over standard input and output, verifies the exact five-tool allowlist, and rejects broader capabilities.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.900
Oracle SQL calculates the feasible product, source, target, quantity, transit time, cost, and stockout risk.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.900
Gemini Enterprise registers the Cloud Run adapter as a custom A2A agent.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.900
The adapter streams A2UI version zero point eight DataParts, while the host owns the native component catalog, layout, accessibility, and interaction model.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.900
The live Gemini result shows the Oracle-governed WATER-SENSE recommendation: move forty-two units from PHX-DC to SEA-FC at stockout risk seventy-four point six.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.900
Gemini renders native approval notes and exact-transfer controls without loading an MCP App iframe.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.900
ChatGPT Developer Mode connects to the dedicated public HTTPS MCP endpoint for the time-bounded synthetic read-only test.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:23.900
Discovery exposes exactly one model-visible dashboard tool with bounded stockout-risk and row-limit inputs; write tools remain unregistered.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.900
ChatGPT calls the tool, loads the versioned UI resource, and renders the Toolkit-labeled dashboard inline.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:37.900
The recommendation, route, quantity, risk score, and model-readable summary match the private Cloud Run and Oracle Database preflight.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:44.900
Claude adds the same endpoint as a custom web connector, verifies its single interactive tool and permission policy, and enables it for a conversation.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.900
The connector uses the same Streamable HTTP server and the same self-contained MCP App resource as ChatGPT.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.900
In a regular browser, Claude invokes the tool and renders the same live WATER-SENSE dashboard inline.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:05.900
The installed Chrome-app surface failed during this test, so the verified claim is deliberately limited to Claude in a regular browser.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.400
The three hosts use different UI trust models.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.900
Gemini receives declarative A2UI and renders native controls.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.400
ChatGPT and Claude receive sandboxed HTML through MCP Apps.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.900
All three share the governed recommendation service, identifiers, Toolkit operations, and Oracle transaction boundary.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.567
Public validation remains synthetic and read-only.

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:29.233
The widget says so explicitly and disables its preview action when no approval handle exists.

00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:33.900
Production approval requires OAuth, durable actor-bound state, least-privileged Oracle access, revalidation under locks, auditing, and immediate removal of temporary anonymous access.

